  "proposed_statement_changes": [
    {
      "id": "thm:path-bands",
      "proposed": {
        "tex_ref": "path-proposed"
      },
      "reason": "The original uniform coverage clause includes local sequences for which \\(\\Omega_\\theta\\) collapses to zero. An explicit certificate is the scalar regular subproblem \\(\\sqrt N(\\widehat b-b)=Z\\), \\(Z\\sim\\mathcal N(0,1)\\), with the smooth coordinate \\(\\Psi(b)=b^2\\), plug-in covariance \\(4\\widehat b^2\\), and \\(b=2/\\sqrt N\\). At \\(\\alpha=0.05\\), its limiting plug-in Wald coverage is \\(\\mathbb P\\{|4Z+Z^2|\\le2z_{0.975}|2+Z|\\}\\), approximately \\(0.8765<0.95\\), although the covariance estimator is consistent in absolute error and the pointwise first-order expansions hold. The same quadratic coordinate is embedded in the regular affine message family \\(g_\\beta(y,w)=y/2+w+\\beta+\\beta^2w\\), whose additive \\(\\beta\\) term retains mean rank and whose \\(\\beta^2w\\) term gives the quadratic treatment contrast. Requiring the compact family to remain separated from the all-zero path covariance is therefore an honest scope restriction; the asymptotic linearity, Gaussian law, and covariance-consistency clauses remain unchanged.",
      "direction": "narrow"
    }
  ],
